A||N||1||Seanh||Small Engine Rebuild Question?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||01-12-2001||11:00 PM||||I am working on a Tecomsua (sp??) 2 stroke engine. It started knocking real bad a while back and just got around to working on it. Now I see why, all the roller bearings between the connecting rod and the journal on the crankshaft have fallen out. I found them all, and am wondering how the hell to put them back in there??? My off the top idea was to place them all in there, one at a time and tie a peice of floss around them and slide the rod on. Any other ideas? Thanks. Also, what the heck would cause them to fall out like that? I was thinking excessive crankshaft end play?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||01-12-2001||11:34 PM||||The last engine that I worked on like that, I used grease to hold the rollers in place. I am sure there is a better way, but I could not think of it.||||reg||1
